use std
into meshpack_test.amni

Imports: os, gfx.meshopt and gfx.meshpack. A standalone program that checks the mesh packer on the CPU, prints one line per check and ends with "meshpack: ok", or "meshpack: FAILED " and the failure count with exit code 1. Already provided and never defined here: `meshopt::decode(src, count, stride, mode, filter, out) bool` (appends decoded bytes to a growable byte list); in namespace meshpack `optimize(idx, nv, out, remap) int`, `remap_bytes(data, stride, remap, used, out)`, `encode_triangles(idx, out)`, `encode_sequence(idx, out)`, `encode_attributes(data, count, stride, out) bool` and `acmr(idx, cache) real` (index lists are whole-number slices, outputs growable lists by reference); `os::read_file(path, out) bool`, `os::write_file(path, data) bool`, `os::arg_count()`, `os::arg(i, out)` and `os::clock_ns()`. A counter `FAILS`; `check(ok, label, detail)` prints "ok " or "FAIL ", the label, a space and the detail, and counts failures. `r3(x)` rounds to three decimals for printing.

`u32at(b, at) int` reads a 32-bit little-endian unsigned number. `ints(b, size)` turns a byte slice into a whole-number list of its size-byte little-endian numbers (size 2 or 4). `put(b, v, size)` appends v little-endian in size bytes to a byte list. `bytes_of(idx, size)` is a fresh byte list of the indices at that size.

`canon(idx, t, out)` appends triangle t of idx rotated so that its smallest index comes first, keeping the order around. `same_tris(a, b) bool` is true when both lists have the same length and every triangle's `canon` matches. `tri_keys(idx, nv)` is a sorted whole-number list with, per triangle, its canonical corners (p, q, r) as p × nv × nv + q × nv + r.

Records: `Rec` holds kind (0 attributes, 1 triangles, 2 indices), count, size, flag and three byte lists: input, extra and reference. `load(path) Rec list` reads the cases file: records one after another until the end, each kind, count, size and flag as 32-bit little-endian numbers and then input, extra and reference, each its length as a 32-bit number and then its bytes. A record that runs past the end makes `load` give what it has and print "FAIL cases file is whole".

`encode_rec(r, out)` encodes a record: kind 0 `encode_attributes(input, count, size, out)`; kind 1 `encode_triangles(ints(extra, 4), out)`; kind 2 `encode_sequence(ints(input, 4), out)`. `wanted(r)` is what decoding must give back: input for kind 0, `bytes_of(ints(extra, 4), size)` for kind 1 and `bytes_of(ints(input, 4), size)` for kind 2. `round_trip(r, stream) bool`: decode the stream with count, size, mode kind and filter 0 into a fresh list; false when decode gives false; for kind 1 `same_tris` of `ints` of the output and of `wanted(r)` at size; otherwise the output equals `wanted(r)` byte for byte.

`p1_p2_p7(recs, dump)`: for every record encode it. P1 counts records whose `round_trip` is true. P2 counts kind 0 and 2 records whose stream equals the reference byte for byte and kind 1 records whose stream is no longer than the reference, also adding up both lengths for triangles. P7: for records with count above 0, flip the stream's byte 1 (bitwise-xor 255) and count those whose `round_trip` is false. When dump is not empty, it writes to that path, for every record, kind, count and size as 32-bit numbers, then the stream and `wanted(r)` each as a 32-bit length and its bytes. Check "P1 round trip" (all), detail passed " of " total and the first failing record's number, kind, count and size; "P2 reference parity" (all), detail with passed " of " total and our triangle bytes " vs " reference triangle bytes; "P7 damaged streams fail" (all), detail with count; when dumping, check "P3 streams written" with the path.

`p4_p5_p6(recs)` takes every kind 1 record with flag 1 or 3 (meshoptimizer ordered it; 3 marks a grid) and at least 1000 triangles (count / 3). For each: idx = `ints(input, 4)`, nv the largest index plus 1, ref = `ints(extra, 4)`; out and remap fresh; used = `optimize(idx, nv, out, remap)`. P4: a = `acmr(out, 16)`, b = `acmr(ref, 16)` and s = `acmr(idx, 16)`; pass when a is at most 1.07 × b; the control passes when s is above 1.5; print "P4 acmr" with a, b and s. P5: first-use order holds when walking out every index is at most the highest seen so far plus 1 (starting from -1); used must equal the number of distinct vertices in idx; with inv[remap[v]] = v for used vertices, `tri_keys` of out mapped through inv must equal `tri_keys(idx, nv)`; data is 12 bytes per vertex, byte k of vertex v being (v × 7 + k) mod 256, and after `remap_bytes(data, 12, remap, used, moved)` the 12 bytes at slot remap[v] equal vertex v's for every used v. The control: idx itself is not in first-use order. P6, only for flag 3 records: bpt = bytes of `encode_triangles(out)` over triangles and sb = bytes of `encode_triangles(idx)` over triangles; bpt under 2 and sb over 4 for the control; print "P6 bytes a triangle" with both. Check once each over all such records (and at least one record; P6 over its flag 3 records, at least one, its detail counting only those): "P4 cache misses within 1.07x of meshoptimizer", "P4 control: shuffled input misses", "P5 first-use order, same triangles, same vertex bytes", "P5 control: shuffled input is not in first-use order", "P6 under 2 bytes a triangle", "P6 control: shuffled order over 4".

`p8()`: a grid of 1000 by 500 quads, vertex (x, y) numbered y × 1001 + x, each quad (a = y × 1001 + x, b = a + 1, c = a + 1001, d = c + 1) giving triangles (a, b, d) and (a, d, c). Shuffle with a seed s starting at 7 that steps as s = (s × 1103515245 + 12345) mod 2 to the power 32: first a vertex renumbering perm (0 to nv - 1, Fisher-Yates from the end: for i from n - 1 down to 1 step s then swap i with s mod (i + 1)), then the triangle order with the same shuffle applied to whole triangles; the index list is the shuffled triangles with every index v replaced by perm[v]. data has 12 bytes per vertex: vertex perm[v] holds x, y and 0 of v as 32-bit little-endian numbers. Time with `os::clock_ns`: `optimize`, then `remap_bytes` with stride 12, then `encode_triangles` of the optimized list, then `encode_attributes` of the moved bytes with used and 12. Print "P8 ms" with each of the four in milliseconds, the total, bytes a triangle and bytes a vertex; check the total is under 700 ("P8 1M triangles packed under 700 ms").

`main()`: the cases path is argument 1 when `os::arg_count()` is above 1, else "hc/test/gfx/fixtures/meshpack_cases.bin"; the dump path is argument 2 when there are more than 2 arguments, else empty. When the file can't be read, check "cases file" false with the path. Otherwise run `p1_p2_p7`, then `p4_p5_p6`. Then `p8()`. Finally "meshpack: ok", or "meshpack: FAILED " and the count and exit 1.
